Third-party components
----------------------

This repository bundles no third-party code, fonts, images or data. Everything
in it is the work of the copyright holder above and is under the License, except
the app icon.

- The designs (the .mcvt packages and their preview images), the sample CVs,
  the translations of the document headings, the closed vocabularies of the AI
  draft, the golden files and the test fixtures were written for this project.
- No font file is distributed. The designs name font families only: system
  families such as -apple-system, Helvetica and Arial, and, in one legacy font
  scheme, Inter. A family the device does not have falls back to the next one.

Used by the project, not included in this repository:

- swift-syntax (https://github.com/swiftlang/swift-syntax), under the Apache
  License 2.0 with the Runtime Library Exception. Swift Package Manager fetches
  it to build the architecture checker (Tools/ArchitectureCheck) and the
  prototype's checker (Prototypes/ADRValidation/checker). The app does not
  contain it.
- Apple's SDK frameworks (among them SwiftUI, UIKit, WebKit, PDFKit and
  Foundation Models) and SF Symbols, which the operating system provides. They
  are used under Apple's terms. SF Symbols may be used only in apps for Apple
  platforms.
- The GitHub Actions actions/checkout and actions/cache (MIT License) and the
  swift container image, which the CI workflow in .github/workflows uses.
- The Swift toolchain and the Swift SDK for Android from swift.org, and the
  Android NDK of the runner image, which the CI workflow's Android job uses to
  build the portable targets. Nothing it builds is distributed.
